{"id": "whpyrenees", "name": "Pyrénées - Mont Perdu", "short": "Pyrénées-Perdu", "place": "France and Spain", "lat": 42.7, "lon": 0.0, "side": "l", "cont": "Europe", "country": "France", "countries": ["France", "Spain"], "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "blurb": "Izard, marmots and vultures on shared France-Spain summer pastures.", "tip": {"id": "sheep", "title": "Leave no flock on the pastures", "text": "Livestock carcasses feed griffon and bearded vultures. Set Domestic sheep to -100% and see how the vultures and bear that rely on them fare."}, "sources": [{"title": "UNESCO: Pyrénées - Mont Perdu", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/773"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Ordesa y Monte Perdido National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ordesa_y_Monte_Perdido_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Bearded vulture", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bearded_vulture"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Pyrenean desman", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrenean_desman"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Alpine marmot", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine_marmot"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Griffon vulture", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Griffon_vulture"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Pyrénées – Mont Perdu", "icon": "ice", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "summer sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Short, bright high-mountain summers power the meadows and shrub heaths above the treeline."}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "winter snowpack", "xh": 0.35, "wiki": "Snow", "desc": "Deep snow covers the high ground for months and, as it melts, feeds the streams and lakes below."}, {"id": "stream", "sp": "clear fast streams", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "transhum", "sp": "seasonal grazing (transhumance)", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.97, "name": "Soil fungi and bacteria", "desc": "Break down carcasses, dung, leaf litter and dead plants, returning nutrients to mountain soils."}, {"id": "calluna", "sp": "calluna vulgaris", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "bilberry", "sp": "vaccinium myrtillus", "xh": 0.32, "desc": "A berry-bearing dwarf shrub of sub-alpine slopes, browsed by deer and its fruit eaten by bears."}, {"id": "nardus", "sp": "nardus stricta", "xh": 0.55}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus sylvatica", "xh": 0.8, "wiki": "Fagus sylvatica", "desc": "A main tree of the humid northern valley forests, giving leaves, buds and cover to deer and stream life.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "chamois", "sp": "rupicapra pyrenaica", "xh": 0.08}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.27, "name": "Roe deer", "wiki": "Roe deer", "desc": "A small woodland deer that browses heather, beech and bilberry in the valley forests."}, {"id": "marmot", "sp": "marmota marmota", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "Hibernating burrow-dweller of the high meadows, reintroduced to the Pyrenees in 1948. It eats grasses and herbs and whistles to warn of danger."}, {"id": "sheep", "sp": "ovis aries", "xh": 0.65, "desc": "The main livestock of the summer pastures. Dead animals left on the mountain feed vultures and other scavengers."}, {"id": "caddis", "sp": "trichoptera", "xh": 0.88, "wiki": "Trichoptera", "desc": "Aquatic insect larvae in cold streams and the favoured prey of the Pyrenean desman.", "ic": "hopper"}, {"id": "desman", "sp": "galemys pyrenaicus", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.3, "wiki": "Red fox", "desc": "Opportunistic hunter with many recorded prey here, including marmots and small mammals."}, {"id": "stoat", "sp": "mustela erminea", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "A slim weasel relative that hunts marmots, hares and small animals even on high ground."}, {"id": "griffon", "sp": "gyps fulvus", "xh": 0.72, "desc": "A large cliff-nesting scavenger that feeds on carrion. It 